WEBVTT

00:00:16.220 --> 00:00:18.378
Storm's coming. And you boys?

00:00:18.379 --> 00:00:21.336
Your daddy? You are
smack in the middle of it.

00:00:27.564 --> 00:00:29.584
Take your brother outside
as fast as you can!

00:00:29.585 --> 00:00:31.091
Now, Dean! Go!

00:00:32.987 --> 00:00:34.931
He wants us to pick
up where he left off.

00:00:34.932 --> 00:00:37.185
Saving people, hunting things...

00:00:37.186 --> 00:00:38.904
The family business.

00:00:43.895 --> 00:00:46.648
Our whole lives have been
searching for this demon.

00:00:47.722 --> 00:00:49.533
Samuel Colt made a gun.

00:00:49.537 --> 00:00:51.722
They say this gun can kill anything.

00:00:52.581 --> 00:00:54.595
We finally know who
this demon's gonna be,

00:00:54.609 --> 00:00:56.569
And now, we know how to kill it.

00:00:57.103 --> 00:01:00.001
More and more demons
are walking among us.

00:01:06.585 --> 00:01:08.222
You're not my dad. Dean,
what the hell's going on?

00:01:08.237 --> 00:01:09.703
I think he's possessed.

00:01:11.158 --> 00:01:12.870
My plans for you, Sammy...

00:01:13.548 --> 00:01:16.272
You, and all the children like you.

00:01:21.876 --> 00:01:24.653
It's inside me. I can feel it. Shoot me!

00:01:24.657 --> 00:01:26.490
I can't hold on to it much longer!

00:01:30.926 --> 00:01:32.873
Why didn't you kill it?
We still got the colt.

00:01:32.877 --> 00:01:34.271
We still have the one bullet left.

00:02:13.365 --> 00:02:14.682
Get back

00:02:14.798 --> 00:02:17.111
Or I'll kill you. I swear to god.

00:02:17.128 --> 00:02:18.612
You won't.

00:02:18.616 --> 00:02:21.740
You're saving that
bullet for someone else.

00:02:24.758 --> 00:02:25.901
You want to bet?

00:02:48.255 --> 00:02:49.772
Oh, my god!

00:02:49.775 --> 00:02:51.103
Dad...

00:02:51.105 --> 00:02:53.653
Did I do this? Dad...

00:02:56.358 --> 00:02:57.880
Dean...

00:03:12.147 --> 00:03:14.350
Significant passenger, space intrusion.

00:03:14.355 --> 00:03:17.300
Unresponsive. B.P. 180 over 50.

00:03:17.315 --> 00:03:20.720
B.P. 100 over 15. Heartbeat 95.

00:03:20.727 --> 00:03:23.341
Tell me if they're okay!
You have to stay still.

00:03:23.345 --> 00:03:24.641
Are they even alive!

00:03:51.497 --> 00:03:52.733
Sam?

00:04:00.007 --> 00:04:01.131
Dad?

00:04:03.108 --> 00:04:04.340
Anybody?!

00:04:10.977 --> 00:04:14.301
Shadow county, nurses' station.
How can I transfer your call?

00:04:15.248 --> 00:04:16.933
Of course.

00:04:16.937 --> 00:04:18.410
I transfer your call.

00:04:21.877 --> 00:04:23.801
Excuse me.

00:04:30.078 --> 00:04:31.652
Hi.

00:04:31.795 --> 00:04:35.323
I, uh... I think I was in
a car accident with my...

00:04:35.688 --> 00:04:37.961
Dad and my brother. I
just need to find them.

00:04:43.556 --> 00:04:44.370
Hello?

00:05:36.927 --> 00:05:37.943
Sammy...

00:05:39.246 --> 00:05:40.422
You look good...

00:05:41.107 --> 00:05:42.241
Considering...

00:05:51.297 --> 00:05:53.022
Man, tell me you can hear me.

00:05:56.836 --> 00:05:57.930
How's dad?

00:05:59.295 --> 00:06:00.410
Is he okay?

00:06:02.147 --> 00:06:03.662
Come on, you're the psychic.

00:06:04.356 --> 00:06:06.481
Give me some ghost
whispering or something.

00:06:07.446 --> 00:06:08.580
Your father's awake.

00:06:10.458 --> 00:06:11.860
You can go see him if you like.

00:06:12.426 --> 00:06:13.672
Oh, thank god.

00:06:16.098 --> 00:06:17.580
Doc, what about my brother?

00:06:18.047 --> 00:06:19.781
Well, he sustained serious injury.

00:06:19.787 --> 00:06:22.191
Blood loss, contusions
to his liver and kidney.

00:06:22.195 --> 00:06:24.101
But it's the head
trauma I'm worried about.

00:06:24.108 --> 00:06:26.320
There's early signs of cerebral edema.

00:06:26.326 --> 00:06:27.860
Well, what can we do?

00:06:27.876 --> 00:06:30.620
Well, we won't know his full
condition until he wakes up.

00:06:32.097 --> 00:06:33.092
If,

00:06:33.285 --> 00:06:34.633
He wakes up.

00:06:35.036 --> 00:06:36.031
If?

00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:38.181
I have to be honest. Screw
you, doc I'm waking up!

00:06:38.186 --> 00:06:40.693
Most people with his degree of injury
wouldn't have survived this long.

00:06:40.906 --> 00:06:42.453
He's fighting very hard.

00:06:42.785 --> 00:06:45.601
But you need to have
realistic expectations, son.

00:06:46.216 --> 00:06:47.633
Come on, Sam.

00:06:47.637 --> 00:06:50.410
Go find some hoodoo priest
to lay some mojo on me.

00:06:50.417 --> 00:06:51.612
I'll be fine.

00:06:54.467 --> 00:06:55.743
Sam?

00:06:57.945 --> 00:06:59.833
All right. Here.

00:07:00.545 --> 00:07:02.273
Give them my insurance.

00:07:04.085 --> 00:07:06.102
Elroy Mcgillicuddy?

00:07:06.876 --> 00:07:09.152
And his two loving sons.

00:07:11.508 --> 00:07:12.651
So...

00:07:14.125 --> 00:07:16.212
What else did the doctor say about Dean?

00:07:16.695 --> 00:07:18.062
N othing.

00:07:19.787 --> 00:07:20.750
Look...

00:07:21.006 --> 00:07:22.731
If the doctors won't do anything,

00:07:23.066 --> 00:07:24.741
Then we'll have to, that's all.

00:07:24.745 --> 00:07:26.473
I don't know. I'll find some...

00:07:27.248 --> 00:07:30.030
Hoodoo priest and lay some mojo on him.

00:07:31.607 --> 00:07:33.361
We'll  look for someone.

00:07:33.368 --> 00:07:34.703
Yeah.

00:07:34.868 --> 00:07:36.130
But, Sam...

00:07:37.355 --> 00:07:39.360
I don't know if we're gonna find anyone.

00:07:39.366 --> 00:07:40.440
Why not?

00:07:41.115 --> 00:07:42.853
I found that faith healer before.

00:07:43.098 --> 00:07:45.403
That was one in a million. So what?

00:07:45.405 --> 00:07:47.623
We just sit here with
our thumbs up our ass?

00:07:47.628 --> 00:07:49.001
No, I said we'd look.

00:07:50.585 --> 00:07:53.122
All right? I'll check under every stone.

00:07:57.738 --> 00:07:58.890
Where's the colt?

00:08:01.556 --> 00:08:02.911
Your son is dying,

00:08:02.916 --> 00:08:05.291
And you're worried about
the colt? We are hunting

00:08:05.296 --> 00:08:07.882
This demon, and maybe
it's hunting us too.

00:08:08.488 --> 00:08:10.850
That  gun may be our only card.

00:08:12.198 --> 00:08:13.592
It's in the trunk.

00:08:14.717 --> 00:08:16.940
They dragged the car
to a yard off of i-83.

00:08:16.948 --> 00:08:20.360
All right, you got to clean out that trunk
before some junk man sees what's inside.

00:08:20.366 --> 00:08:21.701
I already called Bobby.

00:08:21.867 --> 00:08:25.253
He's like an hour out. He's gonna
tow the Impala back to his place.

00:08:25.255 --> 00:08:26.542
All right. You,

00:08:26.737 --> 00:08:29.750
You go meet up with Bobby. You get
that colt and bring it back to me.

00:08:29.757 --> 00:08:31.992
And you watch out for hospital security.

00:08:32.007 --> 00:08:33.502
I think I got it covered.

00:08:39.537 --> 00:08:40.680
Hey.

00:08:42.936 --> 00:08:43.750
Here.

00:08:45.375 --> 00:08:46.693
I made a list of things I need

00:08:46.695 --> 00:08:48.592
That Bobby pick them up for me.

00:08:50.345 --> 00:08:51.290
Acacia?

00:08:52.376 --> 00:08:54.682
Oil of Abramelin? What's this stuff for?

00:08:54.688 --> 00:08:55.670
Protection.

00:09:00.516 --> 00:09:01.622
Hey, dad...

00:09:02.208 --> 00:09:03.622
You know the demon?

00:09:03.806 --> 00:09:07.060
He said he had plans for
me and children like me.

00:09:07.185 --> 00:09:09.151
You have any idea what he meant by that?

00:09:09.885 --> 00:09:11.741
No, I don't.

00:09:22.396 --> 00:09:24.871
Well, you sure know something.

00:09:28.346 --> 00:09:29.731
Oh, man.

00:09:30.075 --> 00:09:32.152
Dean is gonna be pissed.

00:09:37.727 --> 00:09:39.551
Look, Sam, this...

00:09:40.687 --> 00:09:42.680
This just ain't worth a tow.

00:09:47.466 --> 00:09:50.632
I say we empty the trunk,
and sell the rest for scrap.

00:09:53.176 --> 00:09:54.021
No.

00:09:56.581 --> 00:09:58.025
Dean would kill me if we did that.

00:09:59.509 --> 00:10:01.439
When he gets better, he's
gonna want to fix this.

00:10:02.703 --> 00:10:04.491
There's nothing to fix.

00:10:05.248 --> 00:10:07.812
The frame's a pretzel.
The engine's ruined.

00:10:08.555 --> 00:10:10.782
There's barely any
parts worth salvaging.

00:10:11.186 --> 00:10:12.182
Listen to me, Bobby.

00:10:13.395 --> 00:10:15.460
If there's only one
working part, that's enough.

00:10:16.467 --> 00:10:18.220
We're not just gonna give up on...

00:10:22.388 --> 00:10:23.592
Okay.

00:10:24.066 --> 00:10:25.273
You got it.

00:10:27.516 --> 00:10:28.820
Here...

00:10:29.006 --> 00:10:31.192
Dad asked if you could
get this stuff for him.

00:10:33.726 --> 00:10:35.260
What John want with this?

00:10:35.756 --> 00:10:37.490
Protection from the demon.

00:10:41.677 --> 00:10:42.662
What?

00:10:43.175 --> 00:10:45.863
Nothing. It's just... Bobby.

00:10:48.035 --> 00:10:49.451
What's going on?

00:11:05.928 --> 00:11:07.143
Come on, dad.

00:11:08.175 --> 00:11:09.561
You got to help me.

00:11:11.578 --> 00:11:13.891
I got to get better. I
got to get back in there.

00:11:19.775 --> 00:11:21.821
I mean, you haven't
called a soul for help.

00:11:22.557 --> 00:11:24.113
You haven't even tried.

00:11:24.597 --> 00:11:25.992
Aren't you gonna do anything?

00:11:26.787 --> 00:11:28.463
Aren't you gonna even say anything?!

00:11:32.317 --> 00:11:34.500
I've done everything
you have ever asked me.

00:11:35.276 --> 00:11:36.443
Everything.

00:11:36.608 --> 00:11:38.821
I've given everything I've ever had.

00:11:40.787 --> 00:11:43.272
Now you're just gonna sit
there? You're gonna watch me die?

00:11:45.756 --> 00:11:47.772
I mean, what the hell
kind of father are you?!

00:11:55.708 --> 00:11:57.052
What is that?

00:12:03.638 --> 00:12:05.080
I take it you didn't see that.

00:12:36.557 --> 00:12:37.561
Hey!

00:12:37.805 --> 00:12:39.443
I need some help in here!

00:12:41.855 --> 00:12:43.150
I can't...

00:12:43.386 --> 00:12:44.490
Breathe.

00:12:55.266 --> 00:12:57.511
Sammy, tell me you can
freaking hear me, man.

00:12:57.518 --> 00:12:58.703
There's something in the hospital.

00:12:58.707 --> 00:13:00.951
Now, you got to bring me back,
and we got to hunt this thing.

00:13:01.228 --> 00:13:02.292
Sam!

00:13:02.777 --> 00:13:03.912
You're quiet.

00:13:09.137 --> 00:13:10.780
You think I wouldn't find out?

00:13:10.788 --> 00:13:12.530
What are you talking about?
That stuff from Bobby.

00:13:12.535 --> 00:13:15.292
You don't use it to ward off a
demon. You use it to summon one.

00:13:15.588 --> 00:13:17.231
You're planning on bringing
the demon here, aren't you?

00:13:17.236 --> 00:13:19.510
Having some stupid macho showdown!

00:13:19.525 --> 00:13:22.462
I have a plan, Sam.
That's exactly my point!

00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:25.112
Dean is dying, and you have a plan!

00:13:25.318 --> 00:13:26.892
You know what?! You care more about

00:13:26.897 --> 00:13:29.353
Killing this demon than
you do saving your own son!

00:13:29.357 --> 00:13:31.343
No, no, no. Guys, don't do
this! Do not tell me how I feel!

00:13:31.348 --> 00:13:33.792
I am doing this for Dean. How?

00:13:34.115 --> 00:13:35.900
How is revenge gonna help him?

00:13:35.906 --> 00:13:37.922
You're not thinking about
anybody but yourself!

00:13:37.925 --> 00:13:40.260
It's the same selfish obsession!

00:13:40.295 --> 00:13:41.780
Come on, guys, don't
do this! That's funny,

00:13:41.817 --> 00:13:44.020
I thought this was your
obsession too. This demon

00:13:44.066 --> 00:13:45.492
Killed your mother,

00:13:45.497 --> 00:13:48.901
Killed your girlfriend. You
begged me to be part of this hunt!

00:13:48.907 --> 00:13:51.510
Now, if you killed that damn
thing when you had the chance,

00:13:51.517 --> 00:13:53.783
None of this would have happened.
It was possessing you, dad!

00:13:53.785 --> 00:13:54.941
I would have killed you, too! Yeah,

00:13:54.947 --> 00:13:56.733
And your brother would
be awake right now.

00:13:56.735 --> 00:13:58.462
Shut up, both of you! Go to hell.

00:13:58.677 --> 00:14:01.161
I should have never taken
you along in the first place.

00:14:01.166 --> 00:14:03.761
I knew it was a mistake.
I said "shut up!"

00:14:11.578 --> 00:14:13.490
Dude, I full-On swayzed that mother.

00:14:26.096 --> 00:14:27.591
What is it?

00:14:27.596 --> 00:14:29.060
Something's going on out there.

00:14:33.096 --> 00:14:34.982
All clear? Clear.

00:14:36.346 --> 00:14:38.050
Still no pulse. No.

00:14:38.495 --> 00:14:39.960
Still no pulse.

00:14:39.967 --> 00:14:42.561
Okay, let's go again. 360. Charging.

00:14:42.577 --> 00:14:44.833
All clear? Clear.

00:14:45.285 --> 00:14:48.052
Come on, come on... Still no pulse.

00:14:50.087 --> 00:14:51.062
Clear.

00:14:53.747 --> 00:14:56.361
Still nothing. Okay, let's go again.

00:14:57.476 --> 00:14:58.761
Charging.

00:14:58.766 --> 00:14:59.600
All clear?

00:14:59.607 --> 00:15:02.140
Get the hell away from me. Stay back!

00:15:04.588 --> 00:15:06.750
There's no change. Starting cpr.

00:15:06.758 --> 00:15:08.052
I said get back!

00:15:14.377 --> 00:15:15.743
Still nothing.

00:15:23.808 --> 00:15:24.692
We have a pulse.

00:15:25.017 --> 00:15:26.541
We're back into sinus rhythm.

00:15:44.357 --> 00:15:45.511
Don't worry, Sammy.

00:15:46.017 --> 00:15:47.440
I'm not going anywhere.

00:15:48.135 --> 00:15:49.863
I'm getting that thing
before it gets me.

00:15:53.006 --> 00:15:54.270
It's some kind of spirit,

00:15:55.027 --> 00:15:56.211
But I could grab it.

00:15:56.918 --> 00:15:58.012
And if I can grab it,

00:15:58.707 --> 00:15:59.662
I can kill it.

00:16:17.027 --> 00:16:18.493
Can't you see me?!

00:16:19.825 --> 00:16:21.703
Why won't you look at me?!

00:16:23.057 --> 00:16:24.232
Now what?

00:16:27.628 --> 00:16:29.612
Somebody talk to me!

00:16:29.615 --> 00:16:32.751
Say something, please! Can you see me?

00:16:33.675 --> 00:16:34.610
Yeah.

00:16:37.728 --> 00:16:39.812
All right, just calm down.

00:16:40.318 --> 00:16:41.443
What's your name?

00:16:41.448 --> 00:16:42.493
Tessa.

00:16:42.656 --> 00:16:44.312
Okay, good, Tessa. I'm Dean.

00:16:44.827 --> 00:16:46.630
What's happening to me?

00:16:47.548 --> 00:16:48.523
Am I...

00:16:48.796 --> 00:16:50.130
Am I dead?

00:16:50.137 --> 00:16:51.650
That sort of depends.

00:17:02.558 --> 00:17:04.080
I don't understand.

00:17:04.458 --> 00:17:06.622
I just came in for an appendectomy.

00:17:08.777 --> 00:17:10.763
I hate to bear bad news, but...

00:17:11.618 --> 00:17:13.512
I think there were some complications.

00:17:16.048 --> 00:17:18.352
It's just a dream, that's all.

00:17:18.357 --> 00:17:19.860
This is just

00:17:19.866 --> 00:17:21.572
A very weird,

00:17:21.746 --> 00:17:23.810
Unbelievably vivid dream.

00:17:23.816 --> 00:17:24.910
Tessa,

00:17:25.358 --> 00:17:26.662
It's not a dream.

00:17:26.917 --> 00:17:28.471
Then what else could it be?

00:17:30.757 --> 00:17:32.863
You ever heard of an
out-Of-Body experience?

00:17:33.908 --> 00:17:35.982
What are you, some new-Agey guy?

00:17:35.985 --> 00:17:38.712
You see me messing with
crystals or listening to Yanni?

00:17:40.586 --> 00:17:42.413
It's actually a very old idea.

00:17:42.986 --> 00:17:44.651
It's got a lot of different names.

00:17:44.868 --> 00:17:46.122
Bilocation,

00:17:46.626 --> 00:17:48.782
Crisis apparitions, fetches.

00:17:48.986 --> 00:17:50.690
I think it's happening to us.

00:17:51.006 --> 00:17:52.302
If it is...

00:17:53.758 --> 00:17:55.490
It  means that we're spirits...

00:17:56.258 --> 00:17:58.172
Of people close to death.

00:18:00.857 --> 00:18:02.393
So we're gonna die?

00:18:02.526 --> 00:18:03.422
No.

00:18:04.158 --> 00:18:05.232
Not if we hold on.

00:18:05.667 --> 00:18:08.490
Our bodies can get better. You can
snap right back in there and wake up.

00:18:12.377 --> 00:18:14.012
What do you mean you felt something?

00:18:14.015 --> 00:18:15.652
I mean, it felt like...

00:18:16.405 --> 00:18:17.530
Like Dean.

00:18:18.258 --> 00:18:20.563
Like he was there, just
out of eyeshot or something.

00:18:21.158 --> 00:18:23.102
I don't know if it's my
psychic thing or what.

00:18:23.375 --> 00:18:24.840
But do you think it's even possible?

00:18:24.848 --> 00:18:27.300
Do you think his spirit could be around?

00:18:27.627 --> 00:18:29.561
Anything's possible.

00:18:29.877 --> 00:18:31.552
Well, there's one way to find out.

00:18:32.228 --> 00:18:34.832
Where are you going? I got to

00:18:34.835 --> 00:18:37.630
Pick something up.
I'll be back. Wait, Sam.

00:18:37.636 --> 00:18:39.032
I promise

00:18:39.178 --> 00:18:40.901
I won't hunt this demon.

00:18:41.467 --> 00:18:43.513
Not until we know Dean's okay.

00:18:48.857 --> 00:18:50.463
I got to say, I'm impressed.

00:18:50.716 --> 00:18:52.252
With what? You.

00:18:52.626 --> 00:18:55.012
Most people in your spot
would be jello by now, but

00:18:55.015 --> 00:18:56.753
You're taking this pretty well.

00:18:56.758 --> 00:18:58.380
Maybe a little better than me.

00:18:58.657 --> 00:18:59.851
Don't get me wrong,

00:19:00.185 --> 00:19:02.311
I was pretty freaked at first. But

00:19:02.707 --> 00:19:04.873
Now I don't know. Maybe I'm dealing.

00:19:04.878 --> 00:19:06.421
So you're okay with dying?

00:19:06.427 --> 00:19:08.563
No, of course not.

00:19:09.357 --> 00:19:12.512
I  just think whatever's
gonna happen is gonna happen.

00:19:12.745 --> 00:19:14.921
It's out of my control. It's just...

00:19:14.925 --> 00:19:16.201
Fate.

00:19:18.886 --> 00:19:20.232
That's crap.

00:19:21.916 --> 00:19:23.580
You always have a choice.

00:19:24.108 --> 00:19:26.990
You can either roll over and die, you
can keep fighting no matter what...

00:19:27.007 --> 00:19:29.163
<i>Room 237. Code blue. Dr. Christie</i>

00:19:29.167 --> 00:19:31.183
Dean, where are you
going? Just wait here.

00:19:38.927 --> 00:19:40.883
Give me another amp oepi, please.

00:19:49.556 --> 00:19:51.080
Get away from her!

00:19:51.578 --> 00:19:52.540
Still nothing.

00:19:59.456 --> 00:20:01.250
All right. Let's call it.

00:20:01.986 --> 00:20:03.130
Time of death...

00:20:03.297 --> 00:20:05.041
5:11 p.M.

00:20:06.556 --> 00:20:08.491
At least she's not suffering anymore.

00:20:24.015 --> 00:20:24.833
Hey.

00:20:26.537 --> 00:20:29.210
I think maybe you're
around. And if you are,

00:20:30.448 --> 00:20:31.961
Don't make fun of me for this,

00:20:31.968 --> 00:20:33.012
But, um...

00:20:34.886 --> 00:20:36.250
But there's one way we can talk.

00:20:42.178 --> 00:20:43.740
Oh, you got to be kidding me.

00:20:59.808 --> 00:21:00.740
Dean?

00:21:05.935 --> 00:21:07.701
Dean, are you here?

00:21:12.518 --> 00:21:15.081
God, I feel like I'm at a slumber party.

00:21:17.647 --> 00:21:19.190
All right, Sam.

00:21:20.576 --> 00:21:22.342
This isn't gonna work.

00:21:40.238 --> 00:21:41.532
I'll be damned.

00:21:43.088 --> 00:21:45.082
Oh, it's good to hear from you, man.

00:21:46.077 --> 00:21:48.123
It hasn't been the
same without you, Dean.

00:21:48.126 --> 00:21:49.430
Damn straight.

00:21:51.566 --> 00:21:52.732
All right.

00:21:56.266 --> 00:21:57.240
Dean, what?

00:21:59.836 --> 00:22:00.773
" H"...

00:22:02.347 --> 00:22:03.113
"U"...

00:22:09.667 --> 00:22:10.850
"Hunt"?

00:22:11.146 --> 00:22:12.581
What, "hunting"?

00:22:12.586 --> 00:22:14.083
Are you hunting?

00:22:17.708 --> 00:22:21.090
Dean, it's in the hospital,
what you're hunting?

00:22:21.096 --> 00:22:22.892
Do you know what it is?

00:22:24.125 --> 00:22:26.031
One question at a time, dude.

00:22:27.097 --> 00:22:28.361
What is it?

00:22:32.755 --> 00:22:34.791
I don't think it's killing people.

00:22:35.335 --> 00:22:36.793
I think it's taking them...

00:22:38.035 --> 00:22:39.342
You know, when...

00:22:40.438 --> 00:22:41.901
When their time is just up.

00:22:44.636 --> 00:22:46.031
A reaper...

00:22:48.655 --> 00:22:50.143
Is it after you?

00:23:00.616 --> 00:23:02.172
If it's here naturally,

00:23:03.607 --> 00:23:05.191
There's no way to stop it.

00:23:06.166 --> 00:23:07.670
Yeah, you can't kill death.

00:23:08.448 --> 00:23:10.220
Man, you're, uh...

00:23:10.227 --> 00:23:11.350
I'm screwed, Sam.

00:23:15.926 --> 00:23:17.630
No. No, no, no.

00:23:18.577 --> 00:23:20.040
There's got to be a way.

00:23:20.507 --> 00:23:21.900
There's got to be a way.

00:23:22.665 --> 00:23:24.180
Dad will know what to do.

00:23:33.985 --> 00:23:34.803
Dad?

00:24:27.607 --> 00:24:30.010
Hey, so dad wasn't in his room.

00:24:30.157 --> 00:24:31.341
Where is he?

00:24:31.347 --> 00:24:34.081
But I got dad's journal, so...

00:24:34.365 --> 00:24:36.503
Who knows? Maybe there's
something in here.

00:24:45.845 --> 00:24:47.883
Thanks for not giving up on me, Sammy.

00:25:06.046 --> 00:25:07.872
Son of a bitch.

00:25:15.767 --> 00:25:17.271
Hi, Dean.

00:25:18.037 --> 00:25:20.593
You know, you read the
most interesting things.

00:25:21.415 --> 00:25:23.883
For example, did you know that reapers

00:25:23.887 --> 00:25:25.870
Can alter human perception?

00:25:27.785 --> 00:25:28.952
I sure didn't.

00:25:30.945 --> 00:25:34.043
Basically they can make themselves
appear however they want...

00:25:35.118 --> 00:25:36.341
Like, say...

00:25:36.908 --> 00:25:38.283
A pretty girl.

00:25:40.108 --> 00:25:42.363
You're much prettier than
the last reaper I met.

00:25:42.468 --> 00:25:44.732
I was wondering when
you'd figure it out.

00:25:46.077 --> 00:25:47.533
I should have known.

00:25:48.628 --> 00:25:53.382
That whole "accepting fate" rap of yours
is far too laid-Back for a dead chick.

00:25:53.387 --> 00:25:56.901
But, you know, the mother and the body...
I'm still trying to figure that one out.

00:25:57.286 --> 00:25:59.232
It's my sandbox.

00:25:59.487 --> 00:26:01.290
I can make you see whatever I want.

00:26:01.298 --> 00:26:03.370
What is this, like a
turn-On for you, huh?

00:26:03.556 --> 00:26:06.390
Toying with me? You
didn't give me much choice.

00:26:06.398 --> 00:26:08.843
You saw my true form,
and you flipped out.

00:26:09.828 --> 00:26:11.772
Kind of hurts a girl's feelings.

00:26:13.558 --> 00:26:16.580
This was the only way I
could get you to talk to me.

00:26:16.738 --> 00:26:17.760
Okay, fine.

00:26:18.446 --> 00:26:19.383
We're talking.

00:26:20.145 --> 00:26:21.841
What the hell do you want to talk about?

00:26:23.626 --> 00:26:25.480
How death is nothing to fear.

00:26:26.726 --> 00:26:28.442
It's your time to go, Dean.

00:26:30.148 --> 00:26:32.600
And you're living on
borrowed time already.

00:27:31.076 --> 00:27:32.723
What the hell are you
doing down here, buddy?

00:27:32.725 --> 00:27:34.183
I can explain. Yeah?

00:27:34.186 --> 00:27:37.512
You're gonna explain to
security. Come on. You follow me.

00:27:38.647 --> 00:27:39.663
Hey.

00:27:41.515 --> 00:27:43.201
How stupid you think I am?

00:27:46.158 --> 00:27:48.842
You really want an
honest answer to that?

00:28:00.057 --> 00:28:03.513
You conjuring me, John? I'm surprised.

00:28:03.517 --> 00:28:05.621
I took you for a lot of things,

00:28:05.627 --> 00:28:09.683
But suicidally reckless
wasn't one of them.

00:28:10.428 --> 00:28:12.153
I can always shoot you.

00:28:12.628 --> 00:28:14.352
You could always miss.

00:28:15.648 --> 00:28:18.270
And you only got one try, don't you?

00:28:21.208 --> 00:28:22.243
Did you

00:28:22.888 --> 00:28:24.751
Really think you could trap me?

00:28:25.955 --> 00:28:27.473
Oh, I don't want to trap you.

00:28:32.316 --> 00:28:33.700
I want to make a deal.

00:28:40.775 --> 00:28:41.883
Dean, are you here?

00:28:46.585 --> 00:28:48.351
Couldn't find anything in the book.

00:28:51.057 --> 00:28:52.670
I don't know how to help you.

00:28:55.918 --> 00:28:57.760
But I'll keep trying, all right?

00:28:58.518 --> 00:29:00.313
As long as you keep fighting.

00:29:03.898 --> 00:29:05.343
I mean, come on, you can't...

00:29:06.065 --> 00:29:09.361
You can't leave me here alone with dad.
We'll kill each other. You know that.

00:29:18.038 --> 00:29:19.830
Dean, you got to hold on.

00:29:22.478 --> 00:29:24.591
You can't go, man, not now.

00:29:27.205 --> 00:29:29.341
We were just starting
to be brothers again.

00:29:33.397 --> 00:29:34.820
Can you hear me?

00:29:37.008 --> 00:29:38.920
Look, I'm sure you've
heard this before, but...

00:29:40.415 --> 00:29:43.351
You got to make an exception.
You got to cut me a break.

00:29:44.085 --> 00:29:45.651
Stage 3...

00:29:45.656 --> 00:29:46.870
Bargaining.

00:29:49.576 --> 00:29:51.033
I'm serious.

00:29:52.668 --> 00:29:54.592
My family is in danger.

00:29:55.568 --> 00:29:57.491
See, we're kind of in
the middle of this, uh...

00:29:58.068 --> 00:29:59.740
War.

00:30:00.106 --> 00:30:02.850
And they need me. The fight's over.

00:30:02.855 --> 00:30:05.520
No, it isn't. It is for you.

00:30:06.205 --> 00:30:07.813
Dean...

00:30:07.956 --> 00:30:10.961
You're not the first soldier
I've plucked from the field.

00:30:11.645 --> 00:30:13.072
They all feel the same.

00:30:13.708 --> 00:30:15.520
They can't leave.

00:30:15.727 --> 00:30:18.263
Victory hangs in the balance.

00:30:18.307 --> 00:30:19.590
But they're wrong.

00:30:20.538 --> 00:30:23.363
The battle goes on
without them. My brother,

00:30:23.367 --> 00:30:24.771
He could die without me.

00:30:25.035 --> 00:30:26.513
Maybe he will.

00:30:27.247 --> 00:30:28.763
Maybe he won't.

00:30:29.627 --> 00:30:31.820
Nothing you can do about it.

00:30:37.547 --> 00:30:39.503
It's an honorable death,

00:30:40.065 --> 00:30:41.832
A warrior's death.

00:30:42.877 --> 00:30:45.452
I think I'll pass on
the 72 virgins, thanks.

00:30:46.225 --> 00:30:48.361
I'm not that into prude chicks anyway.

00:30:48.366 --> 00:30:49.932
That's funny.

00:30:50.047 --> 00:30:51.470
You're very cute.

00:30:53.395 --> 00:30:55.652
There's no such thing
as an honorable death.

00:30:56.657 --> 00:31:00.082
My corpse is gonna rot in the
ground, and my family is gonna die.

00:31:03.085 --> 00:31:04.371
No.

00:31:07.018 --> 00:31:09.382
I'm not going with you.
I don't care what you do.

00:31:12.336 --> 00:31:13.280
Well,

00:31:13.626 --> 00:31:15.120
Like you said...

00:31:16.175 --> 00:31:17.831
There's always a choice.

00:31:18.265 --> 00:31:20.420
I can't make you come with me.

00:31:20.948 --> 00:31:22.153
But,

00:31:22.818 --> 00:31:24.873
You're not getting back in your body.

00:31:25.618 --> 00:31:27.232
And that's just facts.

00:31:28.206 --> 00:31:29.490
So, yes,

00:31:29.498 --> 00:31:30.770
You can stay.

00:31:30.886 --> 00:31:32.821
You'll stay here for years...

00:31:33.366 --> 00:31:34.702
Disembodied.

00:31:34.855 --> 00:31:36.133
Scared.

00:31:36.245 --> 00:31:39.123
And over the decades, it'll
probably drive you mad.

00:31:40.007 --> 00:31:42.172
Maybe you'll even get violent.

00:31:42.328 --> 00:31:44.003
What are you saying?

00:31:47.075 --> 00:31:49.492
How do you think angry spirits are born?

00:31:50.886 --> 00:31:52.423
They can't let go,

00:31:52.437 --> 00:31:54.183
And they can't move on.

00:31:54.467 --> 00:31:56.513
And you're about to become one.

00:31:57.377 --> 00:31:59.391
The same thing you hunt.

00:32:02.957 --> 00:32:05.101
It's very unsinly,

00:32:05.106 --> 00:32:06.852
Making deals with devils.

00:32:08.788 --> 00:32:11.583
How do I know this
isn't just another trick?

00:32:11.695 --> 00:32:13.311
It's no trick.

00:32:14.486 --> 00:32:16.250
I will give you the colt

00:32:16.646 --> 00:32:18.051
And the bullet.

00:32:18.727 --> 00:32:20.780
But you got to help Dean.

00:32:22.638 --> 00:32:24.543
You got to bring him back.

00:32:25.408 --> 00:32:28.173
Why, John, you're a sentimentalist.

00:32:30.038 --> 00:32:31.443
If only your boys

00:32:31.885 --> 00:32:33.780
Knew how much their daddy loved them.

00:32:34.485 --> 00:32:35.923
It's a good trade.

00:32:37.257 --> 00:32:40.783
You care hell of a lot more
about this gun than you do Dean.

00:32:40.785 --> 00:32:42.032
Don't be so sure.

00:32:42.645 --> 00:32:45.203
He killed some people
very special to me.

00:32:47.386 --> 00:32:49.720
But, still, you're right.
He isn't much of a threat.

00:32:49.728 --> 00:32:52.772
And neither is your other son,

00:32:52.886 --> 00:32:53.990
Of course.

00:32:57.706 --> 00:32:59.181
You know the truth,

00:32:59.185 --> 00:33:00.233
Right?

00:33:01.747 --> 00:33:03.243
About Sammy...

00:33:03.838 --> 00:33:05.270
And the other children?

00:33:05.736 --> 00:33:06.610
Yeah.

00:33:07.126 --> 00:33:08.810
I've known for a while.

00:33:08.818 --> 00:33:12.583
But Sam doesn't, does he?
You've been playing dumb.

00:33:13.135 --> 00:33:15.083
Can you bring Dean back?

00:33:15.675 --> 00:33:17.743
Yes or no.

00:33:17.746 --> 00:33:18.950
No.

00:33:19.968 --> 00:33:21.760
But I know someone who can.

00:33:22.878 --> 00:33:24.210
It's not a problem.

00:33:25.088 --> 00:33:25.973
Good.

00:33:26.688 --> 00:33:28.690
And before I give you the gun,

00:33:29.267 --> 00:33:31.653
I'm gonna want to make
sure that Dean's okay,

00:33:31.667 --> 00:33:33.293
With my own eyes.

00:33:33.295 --> 00:33:35.183
Oh, John, I'm offended.

00:33:35.186 --> 00:33:36.710
Don't you trust me?

00:33:41.507 --> 00:33:42.451
Fine.

00:33:44.025 --> 00:33:47.450
So we have a deal? No, John, not yet.

00:33:47.457 --> 00:33:50.043
You still need to sweeten the pot.

00:33:50.476 --> 00:33:51.802
With what?

00:33:53.816 --> 00:33:57.032
There's something else I want

00:33:57.356 --> 00:33:58.823
As much as that gun.

00:34:00.305 --> 00:34:01.630
Maybe more.

00:34:03.916 --> 00:34:05.862
It's time to put the pain behind you.

00:34:09.055 --> 00:34:10.380
And go where?

00:34:11.775 --> 00:34:12.831
Sorry.

00:34:13.708 --> 00:34:16.050
I can't give away the big punch line.

00:34:22.085 --> 00:34:23.412
Moment of truth.

00:34:25.345 --> 00:34:27.123
No changing your mind later.

00:34:30.247 --> 00:34:31.893
So, what's it going to be?

00:34:52.898 --> 00:34:54.312
What are you doing that for?

00:34:55.326 --> 00:34:56.432
I'm not doing it.

00:34:58.237 --> 00:34:59.691
What the hell...!

00:34:59.698 --> 00:35:01.221
You can't do this!

00:35:01.398 --> 00:35:02.862
Get away!

00:35:03.248 --> 00:35:04.840
What's happening?!

00:35:15.186 --> 00:35:17.100
Today's your lucky day, kid.

00:35:20.896 --> 00:35:21.932
Dean!

00:35:23.015 --> 00:35:24.893
Help! I need help!

00:35:26.668 --> 00:35:27.790
I can't explain it.

00:35:27.975 --> 00:35:29.290
The edema has vanished.

00:35:29.457 --> 00:35:31.442
The internal contusions are healed.

00:35:31.827 --> 00:35:33.090
Your vitals are good.

00:35:34.175 --> 00:35:36.331
You got to have some kind
of angel watching over you.

00:35:36.916 --> 00:35:38.101
Thanks, doc.

00:35:42.505 --> 00:35:44.080
You said a reaper was after me?

00:35:44.086 --> 00:35:44.951
Yeah.

00:35:45.296 --> 00:35:46.390
How did I ditch it?

00:35:46.566 --> 00:35:47.660
You got me.

00:35:48.958 --> 00:35:50.573
Dean, you really don't
remember anything?

00:35:51.018 --> 00:35:51.901
No.

00:35:52.648 --> 00:35:53.753
Except this

00:35:54.067 --> 00:35:55.542
Pit in my stomach.

00:35:56.846 --> 00:35:58.430
Sam, something's wrong.

00:36:01.956 --> 00:36:03.410
How you feeling, dude?

00:36:04.046 --> 00:36:05.271
Fine, I guess.

00:36:06.205 --> 00:36:07.283
I'm alive.

00:36:07.407 --> 00:36:09.141
That's what matters.

00:36:09.545 --> 00:36:10.842
Where were you last night?

00:36:13.607 --> 00:36:15.312
I had some things to take care of.

00:36:15.778 --> 00:36:17.281
Well, that's specific.

00:36:17.966 --> 00:36:19.441
Come on, Sam.

00:36:20.208 --> 00:36:21.840
Did you go after the demon?

00:36:23.797 --> 00:36:24.750
No.

00:36:24.757 --> 00:36:27.352
You know, why don't I
believe you right now?

00:36:33.828 --> 00:36:35.471
Can we not fight?

00:36:37.118 --> 00:36:40.353
You know, half the time we're fighting,
I don't know what we're fighting about.

00:36:40.358 --> 00:36:41.671
We're just butting heads.

00:36:43.157 --> 00:36:45.123
Look, Sammy, I've...

00:36:45.558 --> 00:36:47.391
I've made some mistakes.

00:36:48.918 --> 00:36:51.632
But I've always done the best I could.

00:36:53.446 --> 00:36:55.502
I just don't want to
fight anymore, okay?

00:36:57.445 --> 00:36:59.171
Dad, are you all right?

00:37:02.065 --> 00:37:03.220
Yeah.

00:37:03.708 --> 00:37:05.493
Yeah, I'm just a little tired.

00:37:06.985 --> 00:37:08.801
Hey, son, would you mind, uh...

00:37:09.717 --> 00:37:12.022
Would you mind getting
me a cup of caffeine?

00:37:12.075 --> 00:37:14.242
Yeah. Yeah, sure.

00:37:35.738 --> 00:37:37.203
What is it?

00:37:39.225 --> 00:37:40.533
You know, when, uh...

00:37:41.307 --> 00:37:42.922
When you were a kid,

00:37:44.998 --> 00:37:46.762
I'd come home from a hunt,

00:37:48.155 --> 00:37:51.001
And after what I'd seen, I'd be...

00:37:52.055 --> 00:37:53.631
I'd be wrecked.

00:37:54.478 --> 00:37:56.133
And you...

00:37:57.158 --> 00:37:58.980
You'd come up to me, and

00:37:58.985 --> 00:38:02.140
You'd put your hand on my shoulder, and
you'd look me in the eye, and you'd...

00:38:07.487 --> 00:38:09.451
You'd say, "it's okay, dad".

00:38:17.326 --> 00:38:19.151
I'm sorry.

00:38:20.816 --> 00:38:22.621
Why?

00:38:24.956 --> 00:38:28.753
You shouldn't have had to say that to
me. I should've been saying that to you.

00:38:30.466 --> 00:38:32.122
You know, I put...

00:38:33.355 --> 00:38:37.201
I put too much on your shoulders.
I made you grow up too fast.

00:38:38.896 --> 00:38:41.540
You took care of Sammy.
You took care of me.

00:38:43.187 --> 00:38:44.991
You did that.

00:38:45.705 --> 00:38:47.682
And you didn't complain. Not once.

00:38:52.675 --> 00:38:55.003
I just want you to know...

00:38:56.175 --> 00:38:58.621
That I am so proud of you.

00:39:01.788 --> 00:39:03.711
Is it really you talking?

00:39:03.715 --> 00:39:04.621
Yeah.

00:39:05.035 --> 00:39:06.710
Yeah, it's really me.

00:39:08.617 --> 00:39:10.631
Why are you saying this stuff?

00:39:18.905 --> 00:39:21.791
I want you to watch out for Sammy, okay?

00:39:22.728 --> 00:39:24.572
Yeah, dad, you know I will.

00:39:25.738 --> 00:39:27.130
You're scaring me.

00:39:28.918 --> 00:39:30.890
Don't be scared, Dean.

00:40:28.386 --> 00:40:29.452
Okay.

00:40:42.556 --> 00:40:43.552
Dad?

00:41:04.247 --> 00:41:06.332
No, no, no, it's our dad. It's our dad!

00:41:08.515 --> 00:41:10.771
Okay. Let's try again.
An amp of atropine.

00:41:10.775 --> 00:41:11.651
Come on...

00:41:18.125 --> 00:41:19.721
Okay. Stop compression.

00:41:27.256 --> 00:41:29.263
Come on, come on. Still no pulse.

00:41:30.618 --> 00:41:33.022
Okay. That's it,
everybody. I'll call it.

00:41:34.467 --> 00:41:37.163
Time of death, 10:41 a.M.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
<font color="#ffff00" size=14>www.tvsubtitles.net</font>
